.TH VECTOR 1 "2026-03-26" "vector 0.8.0" "Vector Pro CLI"
.SH NAME
vector \- command-line interface for the Vector Pro API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vector
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vector
is the official CLI for the Vector Pro WordPress hosting platform by BuiltFast.
It provides full access to the Vector Pro API for managing sites, environments,
deployments, SSL certificates, WAF rules, backups, restores, and account settings.
.PP
Output is automatically formatted as tables when connected to a terminal, or as
JSON when piped to another program. This can be overridden with the
.B \-\-json
and
.B \-\-no\-json
flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
API token for this invocation. Overrides the
.B VECTOR_API_KEY
environment variable and stored credentials.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Force JSON output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-json
Force table output.
.TP
.BI \-\-jq " EXPRESSION"
Filter JSON output with a jq expression (built-in, no external
.B jq
required). Automatically forces JSON output. Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-no\-json .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS auth \- Manage authentication
.TP
.B auth login \fR[\fB\-\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]
Log in with an API token. If
.B \-\-token
is not provided, you will be prompted to enter one interactively.
.TP
.B auth logout
Log out and clear stored credentials.
.TP
.B auth status
Check the current authentication status.
.SS site \- Manage sites
.TP
.B site list \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List all sites. Defaults to page 1 with 15 results per page.
.TP
.B site show \fIID\fR
Show details for a site.
.TP
.B site create \fB\-\-customer\-id\fR \fIID\fR \fB\-\-dev\-php\-version\fR \fIVERSION\fR \fR[\fB\-\-production\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR] [\fB\-\-staging\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR \fITAGS\fR] [\fB\-\-wp\-admin\-email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB\-\-wp\-admin\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-\-wp\-site\-title\fR \fITITLE\fR]
Create a new site. Optionally set custom domains for the production and staging
environments. When custom domains are provided, DNS setup instructions and
certificate validation records will be displayed.
.IP
When
.B \-\-wp\-admin\-email
is provided, WordPress will be automatically installed in the dev container on
first boot. The generated admin password is only displayed in the creation
response. Use
.B \-\-wp\-admin\-user
to set the admin username (default: "admin") and
.B \-\-wp\-site\-title
to set the site title (default: "WordPress").
.TP
.B site update \fIID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-customer\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR \fITAGS\fR]
Update a site.
.TP
.B site delete \fIID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Delete a site. Use
.B \-\-force
to skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B site clone \fIID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-customer\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-dev\-php\-version\fR \fIVERSION\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR \fITAGS\fR]
Clone an existing site.
.TP
.B site suspend \fIID\fR
Suspend a site.
.TP
.B site unsuspend \fIID\fR
Unsuspend a site.
.TP
.B site reset\-sftp\-password \fIID\fR
Reset the SFTP password for a site.
.TP
.B site reset\-db\-password \fIID\fR
Reset the database password for a site.
.TP
.B site purge\-cache \fIID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-cache\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR]
Purge the cache for a site. Optionally filter by cache tag or URL.
.TP
.B site logs \fIID\fR \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
View site logs. Options:
.B \-\-start\-time
.IR ISO8601 ,
.B \-\-end\-time
.IR ISO8601 ,
.B \-\-limit
.IR N ,
.B \-\-environment
.IR NAME ,
.B \-\-deployment\-id
.IR ID ,
.B \-\-level
.IR LEVEL ,
.B \-\-cursor
.IR CURSOR .
.TP
.B site wp\-reconfig \fIID\fR
Regenerate wp\-config.php for a site.
.SS site ssh\-key \- Manage site SSH keys
.TP
.B site ssh\-key list \fISITE_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List SSH keys for a site.
.TP
.B site ssh\-key add \fISITE_ID\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-public\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR
Add an SSH key to a site.
.TP
.B site ssh\-key remove \fISITE_ID\fR \fIKEY_ID\fR
Remove an SSH key from a site.
.SS env \- Manage environments
.TP
.B env list \fISITE_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List environments for a site.
.TP
.B env show \fIENV_ID\fR
Show environment details. When a custom domain is set, DNS setup instructions,
certificate status, and certificate validation records are displayed.
.TP
.B env create \fISITE_ID\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-custom\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR \fB\-\-php\-version\fR \fIVERSION\fR \fR[\fB\-\-is\-production\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR \fITAGS\fR]
Create a new environment. DNS setup instructions and certificate validation
records will be displayed after creation.
.TP
.B env update \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-custom\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR] [\fB\-\-clear\-custom\-domain\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR \fITAGS\fR]
Update an environment. If a custom domain change is initiated, the pending
domain change ID and status will be displayed along with DNS setup instructions
and certificate validation records.
.TP
.B env delete \fIENV_ID\fR
Delete an environment.
.TP
.B env reset\-db\-password \fIENV_ID\fR
Reset the database password for an environment.
.TP
.B env domain\-change\-status \fIENV_ID\fR \fIDOMAIN_CHANGE_ID\fR
Check the status of a domain change.
.SS env secret \- Manage environment secrets
.TP
.B env secret list \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List secrets for an environment.
.TP
.B env secret show \fISECRET_ID\fR
Show secret details.
.TP
.B env secret create \fIENV_ID\fR \fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR \fB\-\-value\fR \fIVALUE\fR \fR[\fB\-\-no\-secret\fR]
Create a secret. Use
.B \-\-no\-secret
to store as a plain environment variable.
.TP
.B env secret update \fISECRET_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR] [\fB\-\-value\fR \fIVALUE\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-secret\fR]
Update a secret.
.TP
.B env secret delete \fISECRET_ID\fR
Delete a secret.
.SS env db \- Manage environment databases
.TP
.B env db promote \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-drop\-tables\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-foreign\-keys\fR]
Promote the dev database to an environment.
.TP
.B env db promote\-status \fIENV_ID\fR \fIPROMOTE_ID\fR
Check the status of a database promotion.
.SS deploy \- Manage deployments
.TP
.B deploy list \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List deployments for an environment.
.TP
.B deploy show \fIDEPLOY_ID\fR
Show deployment details.
.TP
.B deploy trigger \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-include\-uploads\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-database\fR]
Trigger a new deployment.
.TP
.B deploy rollback \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-target\-deployment\-id\fR \fIID\fR]
Rollback to a previous deployment.
.SS ssl \- Manage SSL certificates
.TP
.B ssl status \fIENV_ID\fR
Check SSL certificate status for an environment.
.TP
.B ssl nudge \fIENV_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-retry\fR]
Nudge SSL provisioning. Use
.B \-\-retry
to retry from a failed state.
.SS db \- Manage site databases
.SS db import\-session \- Large file import sessions
.TP
.B db import\-session create \fISITE_ID\fR \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Create an import session. Options:
.B \-\-filename
.IR NAME ,
.B \-\-content\-length
.IR BYTES ,
.B \-\-drop\-tables\fR,
.B \-\-disable\-foreign\-keys\fR,
.B \-\-search\-replace\-from
.IR FROM ,
.B \-\-search\-replace\-to
.IR TO .
.TP
.B db import\-session run \fISITE_ID\fR \fIIMPORT_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-parts\fR \fIJSON\fR]
Run an import session. For multipart uploads, provide the completed parts as a
JSON array with
.BR \-\-parts .
Each element must contain
.B part_number
(integer) and
.B etag
(string, as returned by S3).
.TP
.B db import\-session status \fISITE_ID\fR \fIIMPORT_ID\fR
Check the status of an import session.
.SS db export \- Manage database exports
.TP
.B db export create \fISITE_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
Start a database export. Currently only
.B sql
format is supported.
.TP
.B db export status \fISITE_ID\fR \fIEXPORT_ID\fR
Check the status of a database export.
.SS archive \- Manage archives
.TP
.B archive import \fISITE_ID\fR \fIFILE\fR \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Import an archive (.tar.gz) to a site. The file is uploaded and processed
on the server. Files larger than 5GB are automatically uploaded using S3
multipart upload (streamed in parts, no additional flags needed). Options:
.B \-\-drop\-tables\fR,
.B \-\-disable\-foreign\-keys\fR,
.B \-\-search\-replace\-from
.IR FROM ,
.B \-\-search\-replace\-to
.IR TO ,
.B \-\-wait\fR,
.B \-\-poll\-interval
.IR SECONDS
(default: 5).
.SS backup \- Manage backups
.TP
.B backup list \fR[\fB\-\-site\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-environment\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List backups. Filter by site, environment, or type (site, environment).
.TP
.B backup show \fIBACKUP_ID\fR
Show backup details.
.TP
.B backup create \fR[\fB\-\-site\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-environment\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR \fIDESC\fR]
Create a manual backup. Scope can be
.B full\fR,
.B database\fR,
or
.B files
(default: full).
.SS backup download \- Manage backup downloads
.TP
.B backup download create \fIBACKUP_ID\fR
Create a backup download request.
.TP
.B backup download status \fIBACKUP_ID\fR \fIDOWNLOAD_ID\fR
Check the status of a backup download.
.SS restore \- Manage restores
.TP
.B restore list \fR[\fB\-\-site\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-environment\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-backup\-id\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List restores. Filter by site, environment, type (site, environment), or backup.
.TP
.B restore show \fIRESTORE_ID\fR
Show restore details.
.TP
.B restore create \fIBACKUP_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-scope\fR \fISCOPE\fR] [\fB\-\-drop\-tables\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-foreign\-keys\fR] [\fB\-\-search\-replace\-from\fR \fIFROM\fR] [\fB\-\-search\-replace\-to\fR \fITO\fR]
Restore from a backup. Scope can be
.B full\fR,
.B database\fR,
or
.B files
(default: full).
.SS waf \- Manage WAF rules and blocklists
.SS waf rate\-limit \- Manage rate limit rules
.TP
.B waf rate\-limit list \fISITE_ID\fR
List rate limit rules for a site.
.TP
.B waf rate\-limit show \fISITE_ID\fR \fIRULE_ID\fR
Show rate limit rule details.
.TP
.B waf rate\-limit create \fISITE_ID\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-request\-count\fR \fIN\fR \fB\-\-timeframe\fR \fISECONDS\fR \fB\-\-block\-time\fR \fISECONDS\fR \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Create a rate limit rule. Timeframe must be 1 or 10. Block time must be one of:
30, 60, 300, 900, 1800, 3600. Additional options:
.B \-\-description
.IR DESC ,
.B \-\-value
.IR PATTERN ,
.B \-\-operator
.IR OP ,
.B \-\-variables
.IR VARS ,
.B \-\-transformations
.IR TRANS .
.TP
.B waf rate\-limit update \fISITE_ID\fR \fIRULE_ID\fR \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Update a rate limit rule. All creation options are accepted.
.TP
.B waf rate\-limit delete \fISITE_ID\fR \fIRULE_ID\fR
Delete a rate limit rule.
.SS waf blocked\-ip \- Manage blocked IPs
.TP
.B waf blocked\-ip list \fISITE_ID\fR
List blocked IPs for a site.
.TP
.B waf blocked\-ip add \fISITE_ID\fR \fIIP\fR
Add an IP address to the blocklist.
.TP
.B waf blocked\-ip remove \fISITE_ID\fR \fIIP\fR
Remove an IP address from the blocklist.
.SS waf blocked\-referrer \- Manage blocked referrers
.TP
.B waf blocked\-referrer list \fISITE_ID\fR
List blocked referrers for a site.
.TP
.B waf blocked\-referrer add \fISITE_ID\fR \fIHOSTNAME\fR
Add a hostname to the blocked referrer list.
.TP
.B waf blocked\-referrer remove \fISITE_ID\fR \fIHOSTNAME\fR
Remove a hostname from the blocked referrer list.
.SS waf allowed\-referrer \- Manage allowed referrers
.TP
.B waf allowed\-referrer list \fISITE_ID\fR
List allowed referrers for a site.
.TP
.B waf allowed\-referrer add \fISITE_ID\fR \fIHOSTNAME\fR
Add a hostname to the allowed referrer list.
.TP
.B waf allowed\-referrer remove \fISITE_ID\fR \fIHOSTNAME\fR
Remove a hostname from the allowed referrer list.
.SS account \- Manage account settings
.TP
.B account show
Show account summary.
.SS account ssh\-key \- Manage account SSH keys
.TP
.B account ssh\-key list \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List account SSH keys.
.TP
.B account ssh\-key show \fIKEY_ID\fR
Show SSH key details.
.TP
.B account ssh\-key create \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-public\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR
Create an account SSH key.
.TP
.B account ssh\-key delete \fIKEY_ID\fR
Delete an account SSH key.
.SS account api\-key \- Manage API keys
.TP
.B account api\-key list \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List API keys.
.TP
.B account api\-key create \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fR[\fB\-\-abilities\fR \fIABILITIES\fR] [\fB\-\-expires\-at\fR \fIISO8601\fR]
Create an API key.
.TP
.B account api\-key delete \fITOKEN_ID\fR
Delete an API key.
.SS account secret \- Manage global secrets
.TP
.B account secret list \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List global secrets.
.TP
.B account secret show \fISECRET_ID\fR
Show secret details.
.TP
.B account secret create \fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR \fB\-\-value\fR \fIVALUE\fR \fR[\fB\-\-no\-secret\fR]
Create a global secret.
.TP
.B account secret update \fISECRET_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY\fR] [\fB\-\-value\fR \fIVALUE\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-secret\fR]
Update a global secret.
.TP
.B account secret delete \fISECRET_ID\fR
Delete a global secret.
.SS event \- View events
.TP
.B event list \fR[\fB\-\-from\fR \fIISO8601\fR] [\fB\-\-to\fR \fIISO8601\fR] [\fB\-\-event\fR \fITYPE\fR] [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List events, optionally filtered by date range and event type.
.SS webhook \- Manage webhooks
.TP
.B webhook list \fR[\fB\-\-page\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fIN\fR]
List webhooks.
.TP
.B webhook show \fIWEBHOOK_ID\fR
Show webhook details.
.TP
.B webhook create \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR \fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR \fB\-\-events\fR \fIEVENTS\fR \fR[\fB\-\-secret\fR \fISECRET\fR]
Create a webhook.
.TP
.B webhook update \fIWEBHOOK_ID\fR \fR[\fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-events\fR \fIEVENTS\fR] [\fB\-\-secret\fR \fISECRET\fR] [\fB\-\-enabled\fR \fIBOOL\fR]
Update a webhook.
.TP
.B webhook delete \fIWEBHOOK_ID\fR
Delete a webhook.
.SS php\-versions \- List available PHP versions
.TP
.B php\-versions
List all PHP versions available on the platform.
.SS mcp \- Configure MCP integration
.TP
.B mcp setup \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Set up Claude Desktop with the Vector MCP server. Use
.B \-\-force
to overwrite existing configuration.
.SS completion \- Generate shell completions
.TP
.B completion bash
Generate Bash completion script.
.TP
.B completion zsh
Generate Zsh completion script.
.TP
.B completion fish
Generate Fish completion script.
.TP
.B completion powershell
Generate PowerShell completion script.
.PP
See
.B vector completion \-\-help
for installation instructions specific to your shell.
.SH TOKEN RESOLUTION
The API token is resolved in the following order (first match wins):
.IP 1. 4
.B \-\-token
command\-line flag
.IP 2.
.B VECTOR_API_KEY
environment variable
.IP 3.
Token stored in the system keyring (set via
.BR "vector auth login" )
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VECTOR_API_KEY
API token for authentication. Overrides keyring.
.TP
.B VECTOR_API_URL
API base URL. Defaults to
.IR https://api.builtfast.com .
.TP
.B VECTOR_CONFIG_DIR
Configuration directory. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/vector .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vector/config.json
Optional configuration settings.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Authentication error (HTTP 401 or 403).
.TP
.B 3
Validation error (HTTP 422).
.TP
.B 4
Resource not found (HTTP 404).
.TP
.B 5
Network or server error (HTTP 5xx).
.SH JQ FILTERING
The
.B \-\-jq
flag filters JSON output through a built\-in jq processor powered by gojq.
No external
.B jq
binary is required. When
.B \-\-jq
is used, output is automatically set to JSON format.
.PP
Extract specific fields:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site list \-\-jq '.[].id'
$ vector site show 456 \-\-jq '.dev_domain'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Filter with select:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector env list \-\-site\-id 123 \-\-jq '[.[] | select(.status == "active")]'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Count items:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector webhook list \-\-jq 'length'
.fi
.RE
.SS Format Strings
The following jq format strings are supported for converting values:
.BR @csv ", " @tsv ", " @html ", " @uri ", " @base64 .
.PP
CSV output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site list \-\-jq '[.[] | [.id, .name]] | .[] | @csv'
.fi
.RE
.PP
TSV output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site list \-\-jq '[.[] | [.id, .name]] | .[] | @tsv'
.fi
.RE
.PP
URL\-encode a value:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site show 456 \-\-jq '.name | @uri'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Base64\-encode a value:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site show 456 \-\-jq '.name | @base64'
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Authenticate with the API:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector auth login
$ vector auth login \-\-token mytoken123
.fi
.RE
.PP
List all sites:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show site details as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector \-\-json site show 42
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deploy an environment with uploads and database:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector deploy trigger 15 \-\-include\-uploads \-\-include\-database
.fi
.RE
.PP
Import an archive with search and replace:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector archive import 42 site.tar.gz \-\-search\-replace\-from old.example.com \-\-search\-replace\-to new.example.com \-\-wait
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a backup and restore it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector backup create \-\-site\-id 42 \-\-scope full
$ vector restore create <backup_id> \-\-scope database
.fi
.RE
.PP
Block an IP address:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector waf blocked\-ip add 42 203.0.113.50
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a one\-off token without logging in:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector \-\-token mytoken123 site list
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use in a pipeline (auto\-JSON output):
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site list | jq '.[].id'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use built\-in jq filtering:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ vector site list \-\-jq '.[].id'
$ vector site list \-\-jq '[.[] | [.id, .name]] | .[] | @csv'
.fi
.RE
